I now have sufficient information to render my Round 8 verdict. Here is my independent verification summary before issuing judgment:

**Verified:**
- AFAA workshop name and oral acceptance status: confirmed ✓
- Seshadri et al. behavioral rates (AAVE: 10.0%/19.7%, Indian English: 9.9%/20.1%, simulators: 18.8%/39.2%): confirmed ✓
- AAVE success rate 39.4% (≈39%), SAE 50.6% (≈50%): confirmed ✓
- UserLM-R1 affiliation (Meituan/Chinese universities): confirmed ✓
- DialectLLM/MDial (KAIST and Amazon, Jio Oh): confirmed ✓
- PersoDPO (arXiv 2602.04493), Liu et al. (arXiv 2605.02624), Haq & Saldías (arXiv 2604.21152): all confirmed ✓

**New critical finding:** The Seshadri et al. paper itself includes a **"minimal intervention"** — a politeness-limiting behavioral constraint prompt — that causes 11/18 tasks to shift difficulty bins and aggregate success rate to drop from 50.0% to 46.7%. This directly targeted behavioral prompting approach is documented in the primary source paper, yet none of DemoCalib's 5 baselines includes it.

